# ComposeBus WS Endpoint — browser-as-live-peer connector; PLACEMENT UNRATIFIED [SPEC:CXC-WS]

> The WS endpoint is a CONNECTOR in the transport family — a new `transport_registry.py`-idiom
> factory, `type: ws` — not a ComposeServer plugin. Where MQTT/CAN/UART DIAL out to an existing
> fabric, WS LISTENS: there is no broker between the kernel and a browser tab, so the kernel's own
> accept socket is the rendezvous point, and that inversion is the one place this connector family's
> surface symmetry breaks. Each accepted connection is a SINGLETON PERSISTENT PEER following the
> peripheral-attach lifecycle — many browser tabs are many independent peers over one listening
> transport, the same shape as MQTT-with-N-devices, not a new concept. One socket carries a fixed
> lifecycle: connect, PRE-BINDING (no focal bus), select a tenant bus, BOUND, optionally SWITCH
> (config-over-bus REPOINT, one tenant at a time — [CXC-CS-MULTI-TENANCY]'s LOCKED boundary is never
> crossed). Auth is explicitly OUT of v1 and reserved as a named fork. This is a build spec: every
> MUST below carries a machine-checkable acceptance criterion and, where the failure class needs
> eyes, a `verify-human` gate.

---

