## 8. Wire format — the faithful BusMessage envelope

### [CXC-WS-WIRE-FORMAT] MUST carry `BusMessage.to_json()`/`from_json()` verbatim; MUST NOT simplify, rename, or drop fields

- requirement: (MUST, testable) every message the WS connector sends or receives MUST be exactly the
  dict `BusMessage.to_json()` produces (`ns`, `type`, `src`, `ts`, `scope`, `seq`, and, when present,
  `val`/`evt`/`data`), JSON-encoded, and MUST be decodable by `BusMessage.from_json()` unchanged. The
  connector MUST NOT introduce a second envelope shape, MUST NOT rename a field for wire brevity, and
  MUST NOT drop an optional field that `to_json()` would have included. This is [CXC-CBK-CONNECTOR-NEVER-TRANSFORMS]'s
  encode-never-derive rule made concrete for this substrate: encode/decode ONLY.
- requirement: (MUST, testable) a value that `BusMessage.to_json()`'s own `_assert_json_serialisable`
  check would reject (raw bytes, an opaque binary chunk) MUST be rejected identically over WS — the
  connector MUST NOT invent a base64 or binary-frame escape hatch that other JSON substrates (MQTT
  JSON payloads, in-process) do not have. Binary/blob content stays OFF the WS connector entirely, per
  control-on-bus/bytes-off-bus; a `bus://` URL reference (DP-CIO-18) is the existing escape and it is
  reused unchanged, not respecified here.
- requirement: (SHOULD) namespaces carried over WS SHOULD be semantic namespaces only — the same
  restriction the `_assert_json_serialisable` boundary already enforces structurally for any JSON
  transport; this property states the intent explicitly so a reviewer does not have to infer it from
  the byte-rejection behavior alone.
- verify-machine: round-tripping every `BusMessage` field combination (with/without `val`, `evt`,
  `data`) through the WS connector's send/receive path produces a `BusMessage` equal in every field to
  the original; a raw-bytes value raises the SAME `UnserialisableValue` naming the same namespace and
  field the in-process/MQTT paths already raise.
- verify-human: none required — this node's behavior is fully machine-observable (byte-for-byte
  envelope equality).
- status: proposed
- provenance: architect-synthesis — "Wire format: the faithful `BusMessage` envelope, JSON-encoded
  (`ns`, `payload`, `type` STATE/EVENT, `scope`, `source`). Encode/decode ONLY — simplifying the
  envelope is a forbidden transform." (session architect-synthesis #7.) The FIELD NAMES quoted here
  (`val` rather than `payload`, `src` rather than `source`) are corrected against the LANDED
  `BusMessage.to_json()`/`from_json()` implementation (`python/composeio/transport.py`) read while
  authoring this spec, not against the dispatch's paraphrase — the dispatch named the FIELDS'
  SEMANTIC roles correctly; this node grounds them in the actual wire keys so a builder does not
  implement a `payload`/`source` envelope that the real deserializer would then reject.
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-WS]
- see-also: [CXC-CBK-CONNECTOR-NEVER-TRANSFORMS], [CXC-WS-CONNECTOR-INTERFACE]

---

## 9. Subscription — explicit, default-deny, reusing the substrate-agnostic filter model

### [CXC-WS-SUBSCRIPTION] MUST enforce default-deny subscription semantics via `bus.on_message()` + `pattern_matches()`; MUST NOT grant a tenant firehose; MUST NOT depend on `subscribe_pattern()`'s unlanded report extension

- corrected-2026-08-25: (diamond-remediation) the ORIGINAL text of this node claimed the WS connector
  reuses `subscribe_pattern()` itself as its subscription waist. That is structurally impossible:
  `bus.py::subscribe_pattern()`'s callback signature is `(namespace: str, new_value, old_value)` and the
  call itself returns `None` — neither carries `src`/`ts`/`scope`/`seq`, so neither can construct the
  faithful `BusMessage` envelope [CXC-WS-WIRE-FORMAT] requires. Both WS diamond legs (gap-analyzer +
  first-bringup) independently confirmed this and endorsed the actual path below. The requirements are
  corrected to name it.
- requirement: (MUST, testable) a WS peer's subscription is DECLARED via the SAME pattern language
  [CXC-SUB-DECLARE] specifies for every substrate — an ordered list of trailing-glob patterns and exact
  namespaces. An empty declared set means SUBSCRIBE NOTHING, exactly as [CXC-SUB-DECLARE]'s default
  states; a peer that wants every namespace on its bound tenant declares `*` explicitly, it is never the
  connector's default. This requirement is about the DECLARED SET's semantics, not the call the
  connector makes to enforce it — see the next requirement for the corrected mechanism.
- requirement: (MUST, testable) the connector's actual delivery path MUST be `bus.on_message()`
  (registering ONE callback that receives every full `BusMessage` published on the bound tenant's bus)
  filtered, per delivered message, through the SAME `pattern_matches()` helper (`bus.py::pattern_matches`)
  `subscribe_pattern()` uses internally against the peer's own declared pattern list — NOT a call to
  `subscribe_pattern()` itself. `on_message()`'s callback carries the full `BusMessage` object (`ns`,
  `type`, `src`, `ts`, `scope`, `seq`, and any `val`/`evt`/`data`) — every field [CXC-WS-WIRE-FORMAT]'s
  envelope requires — which is why this is the correct waist for THIS connector, not a workaround
  chosen for convenience.
- requirement: (MUST, testable) the WS connector's enforcement point, per [CXC-SUB-ENFORCE]'s table, is
  `broker` (degenerate, in-process-equivalent) — the SAME namespace-matching machinery `bus.py`'s
  in-process dispatch already uses via `pattern_matches()`, since a bound peer and its tenant bus share
  one process's address space. The connector MUST NOT widen its OWN dispatch beyond the peer's declared
  patterns to simplify its own code, mirroring [CXC-SUB-NO-INVERT]'s prohibition on inverting a precise
  substrate into a filter-everything-client-side shape.
- requirement: (MUST, testable) because this connector does not call `subscribe_pattern()`, it MUST
  hand-build its own enforcement report at the point it applies `pattern_matches()` — same shape
  [CXC-SUB-REPORT] specifies (`enforcement: "broker"` for this substrate), never silently omitted. NOTE:
  [SPEC:CXC-SUBFILTER]'s own proposed extension — having `subscribe_pattern()` ITSELF return an
  enforcement report — has NEVER LANDED (confirmed by both diamond legs, no such return value exists in
  `bus.py` as authored); this spec MUST NOT be read as depending on that unlanded extension. This
  connector's report is produced independently, by its own hand-built path, precisely because it never
  calls `subscribe_pattern()` to begin with.
- negative-control: a peer that declares `["ship_condition/*"]` and never declares `system/alert`
  MUST NOT receive `system/alert` traffic even though both namespaces exist on its bound tenant — no
  tenant-wide firehose regardless of how many OTHER peers on the same tenant have broader declarations.
- verify-machine: a WS-specific negative-control test (declare `["ship_condition/*"]`, never declare
  `system/alert`, publish both, assert only the declared one is delivered) exercises this connector's
  own `on_message()` + `pattern_matches()` filter directly. [SPEC:CXC-SUBFILTER]'s SUB-C1
  superset-invariant suite (`tests/subscription/test_superset_invariant.py`) does NOT exist on any
  branch as of this correction ([CXC-WS-EVIDENCE]'s `evidence-subfilter-integration`,
  [DEFECT-SPEC-88-CXC-WS-EVIDENCE-1C623F]) — once authored, this connector becomes one substrate row in
  it, not a new test shape, but that authoring has not happened yet and this node MUST NOT be read as
  claiming it has.
- verify-human: none required — this reuses an already-specified, already-testable mechanism; the human
  gate belongs to [SPEC:CXC-SUBFILTER]'s own acceptance table (SUB-C1) once that suite is authored, not
  duplicated here.
- status: proposed
- provenance: architect-synthesis — "Subscription = explicit + default-deny, reusing
  `subscribe_pattern`; no tenant firehose. Reconcile to spec 57." (session architect-synthesis #8.) The
  ORIGINAL `subscribe_pattern()`-reuse mechanism was corrected 2026-08-25 (diamond-remediation) to the
  `bus.on_message()` + `pattern_matches()` path actually endorsed by both WS diamond legs, per
  [DEFECT-SPEC-88-CXC-WS-EVIDENCE-1C623F]; the default-deny SEMANTICS this node states remain the
  architect-synthesis call quoted above — only the WIRE-LEVEL MECHANISM changed.
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-WS]
- see-also: [CXC-SUB-DECLARE], [CXC-SUB-ENFORCE], [CXC-SUB-REPORT], [CXC-SUB-NO-INVERT], [DEFECT-SPEC-88-CXC-WS-EVIDENCE-1C623F]

