## 16. Evidence — pre-integration questions answered, post-integration slots EMPTY until a real build

### [CXC-WS-EVIDENCE] Pre-integration questions (answered by this design pass) and post-integration evidence (EMPTY — never run)

- pre-integration questions answered by this spec: (1) plugin-vs-connector -> connector, new
  `transport_registry.py` factory, [CXC-WS-CONNECTOR-NOT-PLUGIN]; (2) peer model -> singleton
  persistent peer per connection, [CXC-WS-SINGLETON-PEER]; (3) lifecycle shape -> PRE-BINDING/BOUND
  with an explicit-leave switch, [CXC-WS-LIFECYCLE]; (4) tenant boundary -> exactly one tenant per
  bound peer, kernel-served cross-tenant list, [CXC-WS-TENANT-BOUNDARY]; (5) entry modes -> operator
  list and deep-link, both converging on BOUND, [CXC-WS-ENTRY-OPERATOR]/[CXC-WS-ENTRY-DEEPLINK]; (6)
  auth -> deferred, position reserved, [DD-WS-AUTH-GATE]; (7) wire format -> `BusMessage.to_json()`/
  `from_json()` verbatim, [CXC-WS-WIRE-FORMAT]; (8) subscription -> reuse `subscribe_pattern()`
  default-deny, [CXC-WS-SUBSCRIPTION]; (9) retained replay -> connector-layer requirement, not
  WS-specific, [CXC-WS-RETAINED-REPLAY]; (10) identity -> DEFERRED to [DD-WS-AUTH-GATE] per David's
  2026-08-24 Q3 answer ([DEC-WS-AUDIT-RESOLVED-2026-08-24]) — v1 ships with NO persistence; the
  role-dependent persistence policy is described but not required, [CXC-WS-IDENTITY-POLICY].
- pre-integration questions LEFT open, flagged for David/architect ratify before or during build (not
  silently resolved): the auth gate's own concrete mechanism ([DD-WS-AUTH-GATE], deferred by design,
  and with it [CXC-WS-IDENTITY-POLICY]'s deferred persistence policy); the deep-link URL shape
  ([DD-WS-DEEPLINK-URL]); the focal-bus switch's concrete UX ([DD-WS-SWITCH-UX], referenced to the
  operator-console unit — its connector-side ordering is settled per David's 2026-08-24 Q2 answer, only
  the UI trigger is open).
- evidence-connector-module: EMPTY — `composeio/transport_ws.py` does not exist on `origin/main` as of
  this spec's authoring (2026-08-24); this is a build spec, not a report of landed code.
- evidence-lifecycle-real-browser: EMPTY — no browser tab has exercised PRE-BINDING/BOUND/switch
  against real infrastructure (WS-V3's human gate unrun).
- evidence-tenant-boundary-real-infra: EMPTY — no two-tenant deployment has been observed to confirm
  WS-V4's no-overlap-frame human gate.
- evidence-retained-replay-real-load: EMPTY — no real tab-load has confirmed immediate current-state
  population (WS-V10's human gate).
- evidence-identity-real-reload: EMPTY — N/A for v1 (identity persistence deferred to
  [DD-WS-AUTH-GATE] per David's 2026-08-24 Q3 answer); no real reload/private-window pair has been
  observed and none is required until the deferred policy lands.
- evidence-subfilter-integration: EMPTY/pending — CORRECTED 2026-08-25 (diamond-remediation,
  [DEFECT-SPEC-88-CXC-WS-EVIDENCE-1C623F]). [SPEC:CXC-SUBFILTER]'s SUB-C1 superset-invariant test suite
  (`tests/subscription/test_superset_invariant.py`) does NOT exist anywhere in this repo, on any branch,
  for ANY substrate. The prior text of this slot claimed the suite was "landed and passing for the OTHER
  substrates" — that claim was FALSE, confirmed independently by BOTH WS diamond legs (gap-analyzer +
  first-bringup). [SPEC:CXC-SUBFILTER] itself correctly proposes SUB-C1 as a future test
  (`artifact-readiness: system-design`); the fault was this spec's own evidence prose asserting
  VERIFIED-voice over a dependency that has never landed — the false-"landed"-claim laundering shape the
  defect names. This slot is EMPTY exactly like every other evidence slot below, not partially filled.
- why-empty-matters: per [DX-SPEC-CARRIES-ITS-EVIDENCE], "never run at all" must be a QUERYABLE
  PROPERTY, not something a reader has to already know — every slot above is `EMPTY` explicitly rather
  than simply absent, so a future query against this node can distinguish "not yet built" from "nobody
  thought to record it."
- status: draft
- status-detail: draft — every evidence slot EMPTY by construction; this spec has not been implemented
