**Version**: 0.3 — 2026-08-25, diamond-remediation revision. Both WS diamond legs (gap-analyzer +
first-bringup) independently confirmed six defects pre-land; this revision folds in the corrections:
(1) [CXC-WS-EVIDENCE]'s `evidence-subfilter-integration` no longer claims [SPEC:CXC-SUBFILTER]'s SUB-C1
suite is "landed and passing for the OTHER substrates" — it does not exist on any branch, for any
substrate; marked EMPTY/pending, [DEFECT-SPEC-88-CXC-WS-EVIDENCE-1C623F]. (2) [CXC-WS-SUBSCRIPTION]'s
reuse claim is corrected from `subscribe_pattern()` (whose callback cannot carry `src`/`ts`/`scope`/`seq`
and cannot return an enforcement report) to the actual path both diamond legs endorsed:
`bus.on_message()` + `pattern_matches()`, with a hand-built `enforcement: "broker"` report; this spec no
longer depends on [SPEC:CXC-SUBFILTER]'s proposed `subscribe_pattern()`-returns-a-report extension,
which has never landed. WS-V9's acceptance row is corrected to match. (3) [CXC-WS-BOUNDARIES] row 2 (the
bind-failure row) is corrected for the LISTEN role: `_ws()` only constructs, never binds; the bind
happens later on a background thread inside `start()`, which now raises IMMEDIATELY with the underlying
`OSError` text — never a 5s timeout, never a factory-level `None`. The DIAL-role "return `None`"
contract does not transfer unchanged to this one LISTEN-role connector. (4) a new node,
[DD-WS-CONTROL-FRAMES], records that this spec froze only the `BusMessage` bus-DATA envelope, not the
lifecycle/control op-frame vocabulary — the WS and DOM builds each invented their own; a control channel
is named (selection exchange, subscribe, switch, form-validation request/response, `op`-discriminated)
with its concrete vocabulary flagged OPEN, being finalized by the 2026-08-25 WS<->DOM integration pass.
(5) [DD-WS-DEEPLINK-URL] now records that the build implemented candidate (a) `/bus/<tenant_id>` as a
SWAPPABLE DEFAULT via an injected `deeplink_parser` — not a ratify; the fork stays open. Previously
version 0.2, 2026-08-24, audit-resolved revision. Folds in the end-design-session audit
(`docs/composeserver/AUDIT-ws-endpoint.md`, independent auditor, citations verified) and David's
2026-08-24 answers to its three ambiguous questions, per [DEC-WS-AUDIT-RESOLVED-2026-08-24]:
**Q1** (intra-server, confirmed) — each ComposeBus in the selection list is a tenant bus instantiated
and managed by THIS ComposeServer; the "a different ComposeServer entirely" cross-deployment framing
was the architect's over-reach and is retracted ([CXC-WS-TENANT-BOUNDARY], [CXC-WS-SINGLETON-PEER]).
**Q2** (switch mechanism stays settled, only the UX defers) — David's "a mechanism we have yet to
specify" named only the operator-facing UI TRIGGER for a switch ([DD-WS-SWITCH-UX]); the connector-side
leave-A/pre-binding/join-B ordering in [CXC-WS-LIFECYCLE] remains SETTLED and david-endorsed.
**Q3** (identity persistence deferred) — `localStorage <-> NVS` identity persistence is DEFERRED until
a login mechanism exists, explicitly coupled to [DD-WS-AUTH-GATE]; [CXC-WS-IDENTITY-POLICY] is
downgraded from a v1 MUST-persist to a deferred policy description, and v1 ships with NO identity
persistence. Corrections C1-C4 from the audit are applied: **C1** [CXC-WS-TENANT-BOUNDARY] carries
David's re-litigable caveat (line 25921) as an `invalidating_assumption`, distinguishing
one-bus-per-connection-at-an-instant (firm) from the one-tenant-model-survives-real-multi-tenancy
question (re-litigable), and [CXC-WS-ACCEPTANCE]'s WS-V4 gate language is scoped to the firm part only.
**C2** [CXC-WS-ENTRY-DEEPLINK] is re-tagged `architect-synthesis` (the deep-link entry mode was the
architect's synthesis; David described only the operator flow). **C3** the provenance strings on
[CXC-WS-CONNECTOR-NOT-PLUGIN], [CXC-WS-SINGLETON-PEER], [CXC-WS-LIFECYCLE], and [CXC-WS-ENTRY-OPERATOR]
now quote David's ACTUAL words, with the architect's elaboration explicitly marked as the author's
set-across-a-switch default is flagged `architect-synthesis`, pointing at [DD-WS-SWITCH-UX] as the open
fork it belongs to. Previously version 0.1, 2026-08-24, initial build spec, authored from the
composeio-hardware-architect's dispatch (connector-not-plugin, singleton persistent peer, the
connect/pre-binding/select/bound/switch lifecycle, per-tenant boundary inside [CXC-CS-MULTI-TENANCY]'s
LOCKED contract, operator/deep-link entry modes, deferred auth, `BusMessage`-faithful wire format,
connector-layer retained replay, and role-dependent peer identity) as MUST/SHOULD predicates with
`verify-machine`/`verify-human` acceptance tiers, per [DX-SPEC-CARRIES-ITS-EVIDENCE], mirroring
[SPEC:CXC-CS-LOADER]'s build-spec convention.
**Version 0.4** — 2026-08-25, corpus-hygiene revision: [DD-WS-CONTROL-FRAMES] moves `open` -> `decided`.
The control-frame vocabulary shipped and landed on `origin/main` (`transport_ws.py` commit `d95aee1` and
its ancestors); this revision folds in the settled `ws`-discriminated vocabulary (verbs, error codes, the
frozen `type in {state,event}` bus-data boundary, and the DOM-layer `validate_config`/`config_result`
extension riding the same channel), verified directly against the landed code, and corrects the node's
own pre-integration `op`-discriminator description to the actual `ws` key the build converged on.

**Status**: Draft — awaiting architect/David ratify on TWO remaining open forks: [DD-WS-DEEPLINK-URL] (the
deep-link URL shape — the build runs candidate (a) as a swappable default meanwhile) and [DD-WS-SWITCH-UX]
(the focal-bus switch mechanism, referenced to the operator-console unit). [DD-WS-CONTROL-FRAMES] is now
DECIDED (see Version 0.4 above — the control-frame vocabulary landed and is verified against the code).
[DD-WS-AUTH-GATE] (auth position, deferred, david-ruled: out of v1, "way way overkill for right now")
and [CXC-WS-IDENTITY-POLICY] (deferred with it, per Q3) are both settled-deferred, not open forks
awaiting a lean.
The `david-ruling`-tagged nodes now number SIX, matching the six numbered session rulings exactly (no
double-count): [CXC-WS-CONNECTOR-NOT-PLUGIN], [CXC-WS-SINGLETON-PEER], [CXC-WS-LIFECYCLE],
[CXC-WS-TENANT-BOUNDARY], [CXC-WS-ENTRY-OPERATOR], [DD-WS-AUTH-GATE] — each now quoting David's actual
words where the provenance string quotes him, with any architect elaboration explicitly marked as
framing. [CXC-WS-ENTRY-DEEPLINK] moved to `architect-synthesis` (C2). The `architect-synthesis`-tagged
nodes ([CXC-WS-WIRE-FORMAT], [CXC-WS-SUBSCRIPTION], [CXC-WS-RETAINED-REPLAY],
[CXC-WS-IDENTITY-POLICY], [CXC-WS-ENTRY-DEEPLINK]) carry the architect's mechanics falling out of that
